# The data migrations, in the order they are run. One file name per line.
#
# A deploy runs every script listed here that the database has not recorded
# in the `dataMigrations` collection, top to bottom, with `APPLY = true`,
# before the new version starts (deploy/production/files/usr/local/sbin/
# cocoso-deploy). A script that throws stops the deploy.
#
# Adding a migration: put the script in this folder and add its name at the
# END of this list. Never reorder or rename a line that has been released;
# the name is how the database remembers it. `npm run check:migrations`
# fails when a script is missing here or listed twice.
#
# A script must be idempotent, and must throw when it cannot do its job.
#
# `manual` after a name: the deploy does not run it, only says that it is
# waiting. Use it for scripts that delete data or need a decision. Give such
# a script a dry run (change nothing unless APPLY is set) and run it with
#
#   deploy/production/run-mongosh.sh <admin>@<server> scripts/migrations/<name>            # dry run
#   deploy/production/run-mongosh.sh <admin>@<server> scripts/migrations/<name> --apply
#
# which records it as run.

